BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20230207T210000Z
DTEND:20230207T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260815T183631Z
UID:6637-13037929@uga.view.usg.edu
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260814T180902Z
DESCRIPTION:Title: Learning to Solve Combinatorial Optimization Problems.\n
 Speaker: Daniel Mckenzie\,  Colorado School of Mines\nAbstract: Many high-s
 takes decision problems can be phrased as combinatorial optimization proble
 ms. In practice\, the coefficients of such problems might be unknown or unc
 ertain\, leading one to consider learning them from available data. The pri
 mary obstacle to doing so is making sense of the derivative of a solution t
 o a discrete optimization problem with respect to these coefficients. We di
 scuss one way to do so using a continuous relaxation\, and propose a fast t
 raining algorithm exploiting Three-Operator Splitting.\n——————
LAST-MODIFIED:20260814T180904Z
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Dr. Daniel Mckenzie's Talk
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
