BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20230131T210000Z
DTEND:20230131T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260815T183631Z
UID:6637-13483759@uga.view.usg.edu
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260814T180903Z
DESCRIPTION:itle: An Efficient and Effective FEM Solver for Diffusion Equat
 ion with Strong Anisotropy\nSpeaker: Dr. Lin Mu\, University of Georgia\nAb
 stract: The Diffusion equation with strong anisotropy has broad application
 s. In this project\, we discuss numerical solution of diffusion equations w
 ith strong anisotropy on meshes not aligned with the anisotropic vector fie
 ld\, focusing on application to magnetic confinement fusion. In order to re
 solve the numerical pollution for simulations on a non-anisotropy-aligned m
 esh and reduce the associated high computational cost\, we developed a high
 -order discontinuous Galerkin scheme with an efficient preconditioner. The 
 auxiliary space preconditioning framework is designed by employing a contin
 uous finite element space as the auxiliary space for the discontinuous fini
 te element space. An effective line smoother that can mitigate the high-fre
 quency error perpendicular to the magnetic field has been designed by a gra
 ph-based approach to pick the line smoother that is approximately perpendic
 ular to the vector fields when the mesh does not align with anisotropy. Num
 erical experiments for several benchmark problems are presented to validate
  the effectiveness and robustness.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260814T180904Z
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Applied Math Seminar: Dr. Lin Mu will give a talk
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
